  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 3 October 2003, the matter described above is lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reasons:\r\n\r\nThe proposed extension to the dwellinghouse with rear dormer dimensions of 3.58m long by 2.9m deep with a height of 2.3m, that adds 11.93m3, and the existing single storey extension of 37.48m3 and parapet of 0.23m3, provides a total volume of 49.64m3, qualifies as Class B permitted development within Part 1 of Schedule 2 of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995. \r\n\r\nThe proposed rear roof extension therefore, does not require planning permission.\r\n"
